      "descriptions": [
        {
          "description": "Patients included in the “CFB-GBM” dataset correspond to 264 patients with glioblastoma involved in the clinical routine.\n\nPre-treatment MRI (t0) was acquired for all patients. The sequences, such as T1Gd, T1 anatomical, T1 gradient echo, T2 anatomical, T2-FLAIR, T2* or diffusion weighted imaging, were included, depending on their availability. In addition, post-treatment MRI at different times (t1 and t2) were obtained, if available. For some patients, we have also included treatment imaging, such as CTscan, radiotherapy dose and tumor delineation. \n\nClinical data : survival, age, WHO status, gender, height, weight, IDH status and MGMT methylation. \nSurgery criteria, RT dose and machine, fractions. \nCTscan machine, MRI machine, and the delay between the t1 and t2 MRI and t0 MRI. \nPotential research applications of the dataset:\n\nAI model development for: \n\nOutcome prediction [1]\nTumor segmentation and evolution after treatment\nMRI generation\nSpatial analysis of the tumor evolution using RT dose by a pixel to pixel analysis.",
          "descriptionType": "Abstract",
          "lang": null
        }
